    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/GeneratedFormatterCollector.cs",
      "line": 85,
      "description": "Explicit interface implementation detection for IMessagePackSerializationCallbackReceiver checks m.ExplicitInterfaceImplementations.Length > 0 && (m.Name == \"OnBeforeSerialize\" || m.Name == \"OnAfterDeserialize\"). In Roslyn C#, an explicit interface implementation's IMethodSymbol.Name is prefixed with the interface name (e.g. \"MessagePack.IMessagePackSerializationCallbackReceiver.OnBeforeSerialize\"), so m.Name never equals \"OnBeforeSerialize\" or \"OnAfterDeserialize\". Consequently needsCast is always false, causing generated formatter code to call value.OnBeforeSerialize()/OnAfterDeserialize() without casting and fail to compile (CS1061). It also misses base-type implementations and conflates needsCastOnBefore with needsCastOnAfter.",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/GeneratedFormatterCollector.cs",
      "line": 47,
      "description": "GeneratedFormatterCollector.Collect never validates that the user-declared formatter class itself is non-abstract, non-generic, accessible, and has an accessible parameterless constructor. Because GeneratorUtilities.cs L38 bypasses FormatterDescriptor.TryCreate for [GeneratedMessagePackFormatter] classes, declaring an abstract or generic partial formatter (or one with a custom parameterized/private constructor) produces uncompilable GeneratedMessagePackResolver code (CS0144, CS0246/CS0305, or CS7036/CS0122) instead of a diagnostic.",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/GeneratedFormatterCollector.cs",
      "line": 293,
      "description": "IsPartial only checks the partial modifier on the formatter symbol itself and ignores symbol.ContainingType, whereas FormatterTemplate and StringKeyFormatterTemplate emit partial wrappers for all enclosing types via EmitNestingTypesAndNamespaces. A partial formatter nested inside a non-partial class fails with C# compiler error CS0260 instead of reporting MsgPack019.",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/GeneratedFormatterCollector.cs",
      "line": 267,
      "description": "GetInstanceMembers deduplicates seen.Add(member.Name) before checking accessibility, and IsPublicReadWrite (L279-281) only inspects property.GetMethod/SetMethod on the most-derived symbol. As a result, a private field or property on a derived type hides and drops a same-named public read-write member on its base type, and a public virtual read-write property whose derived class overrides only get (or only set) has null SetMethod (or GetMethod) on the overriding symbol and is erroneously skipped in contractless mode or rejected with MsgPack022 in surrogate mode.",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/GeneratedFormatterCollector.cs",
      "line": 171,
      "description": "CreateSurrogateMembers accepts negative integer keys (e.g. [Key(-1)] passes 'key is not (int or string)') without reporting a diagnostic, and allows omitting or [IgnoreMember]-excluding C# 'required' members of the formatted type (also skipped in contractless mode if get-only/non-public), both of which cause the generated formatter to fail compilation (invalid array formatter code or CS9035 on 'new T()'). Similarly, L77 skips the accessible parameterless constructor check for structs, emitting uncompilable 'new T()' (CS0122) if an external C# 10+ struct defines a private/internal parameterless constructor.",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/Analyzers/MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.cs",
      "line": 382,
      "description": "MsgPack019-MsgPack022 are added to MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.SupportedDiagnostics, but MsgPack00xMessagePackAnalyzer.Initialize contains no analysis logic for [GeneratedMessagePackFormatter]; diagnostics are only emitted by MessagePackGenerator. Analyzer-only execution never reports MsgPack019-MsgPack022, and if Options.IsGeneratingSource is false (MessagePackGenerator.cs L135), the partial formatter body is not generated, causing CS0535 on IMessagePackFormatter<T>.",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/MessagePackGenerator.cs",
